SUMMARY:In The Other Room: Brian Bates
LOCATION:Alpharetta
DESCRIPTION:Comedian Brian Bates worked for nearly 20 years in corporate Am
 erica until at the age of 43\, he gave up his day job to pivot into a caree
 r as a stand-up comedian. Since then\, the Nashville based comedian has bee
 n touring the country performing at comedy clubs\, theaters\, corporate eve
 nts\, and churches. Brian has released two Dry Bar Comedy specials\, titled
  Uber Important and Hello Folks. His latest special\, titled Worried\, was 
 released in July 2026 on the Nateland Entertainment YouTube channel. As an 
 originating member of the highly popular The Nateland Podcast\, Brian serve
 d as a host and producer during the show’s six-year run. He now works wit
 h fellow comedians Aaron Weber and Dusty Slay as one of the hosts and produ
 cers of The Public Figures Podcast\, heard by thousands of listeners each w
 eek. He performs regularly on the legendary Grand Ole Opry show and can be 
 heard frequently on Pure Comedy Channel 98 on SiriusXM satellite radio. In 
 addition to stand-up comedy\, Brian made his acting debut appearing in two 
 episodes of the 2022 Amazon sitcom Sprung. He most recently appeared in the
  2026 Nate Bargatze movie The Breadwinner. A native Tennessean\, Brian resi
 des in Nashville\, TN\, with his wife\, four-year old daughter and a seven-
 pound maltipoo who all regularly provide amusing material to incorporate in
  his act.\n\nThere is a two-item per person minimum in the Showroom\, which
  can be fulfilled with any food or drink items from the menu.\n\nPLEASE NOT
 E: Food and drinks purchased in the bar and lounge do not count towards the
  two-item minimum.\n\nManagement reserves the right to prevent customers fr
 om entering the facility who they deem disruptive or dangerous to other pat
 rons.\nMore info: https://comedyatlas.app/comedy-atlas/event/in-the-other-r
 oom-brian-bates/
